        <h2>2. What data we collect and why</h2>
        <h3>Contact form</h3>
        <p>
            When you use the contact form on our website, we collect the following data you
            voluntarily provide:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>First name and last name</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Company name (optional)</li>
            <li>The content of your message</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            In addition, our form processor (Netlify Forms) automatically records technical
            data including your IP address, browser user-agent, and the date and time of
            submission.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Article 6(1)(f) GDPR — processing is necessary for
            our legitimate interest in responding to your enquiry. We do not use contact form
            submissions for marketing without your separate, explicit consent.
        </p>

        <h3>Website traffic</h3>
        <p>
            We do not use any analytics, tracking pixels, or third-party scripts that monitor
            visitor behaviour. No cookies are set for analytics purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Who we share your data with</h2>
        <p>
            We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data. We share data only with the
            following sub-processors, strictly for the purposes described above:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong> (USA) — website hosting and form processing.
                Netlify is self-certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, which the
                European Commission has recognised as providing adequate protection. See
                <a href="https://www.netlify.com/gdpr-ccpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">netlify.com/gdpr-ccpa</a>.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Your data is not transferred to any other third country unless an adequate
            protection mechanism is in place.
        </p>

        <h2>4. How long we keep your data</h2>
        <p>
            Contact form submissions are retained in Netlify Forms for
            <strong>6 months</strong> from the date of receipt, after which they are
            permanently deleted. If your enquiry results in an ongoing business relationship,
            data relevant to that relationship is retained for as long as legally required.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            This website does not use cookies for analytics or marketing purposes. The CMS
            administration area (<code>/admin/</code>) uses session cookies for authentication;
            these are only set for authorised administrators and are not visible to ordinary
            website visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the GDPR, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Right of access</strong> — request a copy of the data we hold about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate data.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — request deletion of your data where no legal basis for retention exists.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to restriction</strong> — ask us to restrict processing in certain circumstances.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to object</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to withdraw consent</strong> — if processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:info@onyx-biopartners.com">info@onyx-biopartners.com</a>.
            We will respond within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
            You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Latvian data protection
            supervisory authority:
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Datu valsts inspekcija (Data State Inspectorate)</strong><br />
            Blaumaņa iela 11/13-11, Rīga, LV-1011, Latvia<br />
            <a href="https://www.dvi.gov.lv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.dvi.gov.lv</a>
        </p>

